{"title":"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/69161dd19a510901853faa798b75d9993bbc13de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} \\sin x + \\log_{10} \\cos x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"17\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/753c6a6868ea88d924600b30e23496ad232c2834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) = \\frac{1}{2} (\\log_{10} n - 1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"285\" height=\"37\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the properties of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithm\" title=\"Logarithm\">logarithms</a>, we can simplify the first equation to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c57324e9d42bba11788d3e6bbb628cd4830f5d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} \\sin x + \\log_{10} \\cos x = \\log_{10}(\\sin x \\cos x) = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc278590c1d813f4bd28263eb411e3cf6eedfc08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin x \\cos x = \\frac{1}{10}.\\qquad (*)\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now, manipulate the second equation.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f892ba91ec3c705891570b7890766141f4f9caa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}(\\log_{10} n - \\log_{10} 10) \\\\ \\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) &amp;= \\left(\\log_{10} \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}\\right) \\\\ \\sin x + \\cos x &amp;= \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}} \\\\ (\\sin x + \\cos x)^{2} &amp;= \\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}\\right)^2 \\\\ \\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x +2 \\sin x \\cos x &amp;= \\frac{n}{10} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"403\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p>By the Pythagorean identities, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/3/4d3cb5dd5fb37bf2356133cf745b0f5c6cfb9088.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin ^2 x + \\cos ^2 x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />, and we can substitute the value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06dc918f8b7700e8637454c2d98382de60651e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"76\" height=\"12\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b174b6793673b39eb92f426d260eed103cc24fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2\\left(\\frac{1}{10}\\right) = \\frac{n}{10} \\Longrightarrow n = \\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"251\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Examining the first equation, we simplify as the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244271621473bf2b40c6c36226c7612548a8403f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10} \\sin x \\cos x = -1\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/37690d5b0edf872355cfe4b53bec07f97137d819.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\sin x \\cos x = \\frac{1}{10}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>With this in mind, examining the second equation, we may simplify as the following (utilizing logarithm properties):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12cc7f67da5d073bd83725a504bc06d8c677ad77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) = \\frac{1}{2} (\\log_{10} n - \\log_{10} 10)\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff79d69669b1a22ec501b1c635105823387cd75d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) = \\frac{1}{2} (\\log_{10} \\frac{n}{10})\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85ac02d055a94c12a9ebfd09a15f1721e9766796.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x) = \\log_{10} \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>From here, we may divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e461509767c74abcd2474173837b689a332e2c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> and then proceed with the change-of-base logarithm property:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b6181ae78a1e39a3c7e576c5228a996da6a1b0fd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac{\\log_{10} \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}}{\\log_{10} (\\sin x + \\cos x)}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad046a24771363abfaf1d5b5e62827a8dfa518db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 1 = \\log_{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus, exponentiating both sides results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/7/e679015726ad6139b54f6f8185db0fdec50e47a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x + \\cos x = \\sqrt{\\frac{n}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"160\" height=\"43\" />. Squaring both sides gives us \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b3379e2ab5167113ae7d64e1c19116347b34ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin^2 x + 2\\sin x \\cos x + \\cos^2 x = \\frac{n}{10}\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>Via the Pythagorean Identity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a958fb1f7b5b87ef62ed4a2205643ef36cb3df4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff29d659880c801c76bffc7bebe4b6060bf10df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sin x \\cos x$\" width=\"88\" height=\"12\" /> is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d129a7b3c0bf9fbd0693afdd426a66d2a0a8c3ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, via substitution. Thus, substituting these results into the current equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3765fd42bae45027a166e399c0275579cec046cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{n}{10}\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cda22f7f22ef62571d9e2309024f858054c58e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{6}{5} = \\frac{n}{10}\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Using simple cross-multiplication techniques, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10e827e4f8af12dceceb7e6382ed7aa0eeb7b9ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5n = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590f40f72d868e38b4364395b4564ae8afd010d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />.\n~ nikenissan\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the first equation, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/275fb3adfe4de3aff77e252c3762aa67d0c615fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)*\\cos(x)=10^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"19\" />. We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f554005f137d0a7c320ebc8fe7e6e79573fd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2ebc0c95a9ef21a14f5301c4a464b10aa4c0904.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5ddead811ba6ada6afc17241b5b5844a8a52f481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=\\frac{1}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"37\" />. By the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3219d16158f4b68175e655cd13eb32fe26ea845c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2x+\\cos^2x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"17\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb41a338501ac2431badf6cf14cc97e8f8b64ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />. Solving this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/4260ce52b7a5502565e116a90d9066b52afb8ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b=\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"104\" height=\"43\" />. So we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f1d95883a27813965a4e92d36e19b130ec0bd1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{10}}\\right)=\\frac12(\\log(n)-1)\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b227c82d3c083090a1198f9ac9a17be1a6df3f23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\log\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{10}}\\right)=\\log(n)-1\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32039fe5fa0eba675edd0b489f38f033a35b600.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log\\left(\\frac{12}{10}\\right)+1=\\log(n)\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9e4d69abb90551719132c16216a968a0fd98de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log\\left(\\frac{12}{10}\\right)+\\log(10)=\\log(n)\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768f4e08d203763c536c4947e8959eef032d7f1e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log\\left(\\frac{12}{10}\\times 10\\right)=\\log(12)=\\log(n)\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>From here it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4ff0485c5c270a4d41e9b6b42248b21652ac817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n=012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/6/f76387eb36c59135dbc7e4fe856dfff5e38d0919.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{x} = \\log_{10}{x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" /> Through basic log properties, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe7e1ec1c5db10c9443f70c2a846bef863c9e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{a} + \\log{b} = \\log{(ab)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"20\" /> Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743ea5c2374fece5760d9724bb5b663f576b29cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log{(\\sin{x})} + \\log{(\\cos{x})} = \\log{(\\sin{x}\\cos{x})} = -1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"373\" height=\"20\" /> Simplifying, we get:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\log{(\\sin{x}\\cos{x})} &amp;= -1 \\\\\n\\sin{x}\\cos{x} &amp;= 10^{-1} = \\frac{1}{10}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Next, we can manipulate the second equation to get:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\log{(\\sin{x} + \\cos{x})} &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}(\\log{n}-1) \\\\\n2\\log{(\\sin{x} + \\cos{x})} &amp;= \\log{n}-1 \\\\\n\\log{(\\sin{x} + \\cos{x})^2} + 1 &amp;= \\log{n}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/adeb5230e3599019ad94eaf4e351b3347bb9e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin{x} + \\cos{x})^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" /> we get:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*}\n\\log{(\\sin^2{x} + \\cos^2{x} + 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x})} + 1 &amp;= \\log{n} \\\\\n\\log{(1 + 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x})} + 1 &amp;= \\log{n} \\\\\n\\log{(1 + \\frac{2}{10})} + \\log{10} &amp;= \\log{n} \\\\\n\\log{(\\frac{12}{10} \\cdot 10)} = \\log{n} \\\\\n\\log{12} = \\log{n}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Finally, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbceec32202e1ef2b49e924ea029ab3bb15c0d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{012}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ Cheetahboy93\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I\" title=\"2003 AIME I\">2003 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2003 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 310/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9146/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.819      1 -total\n 57.30%    7.345      1 Template:AIME_box\n 40.11%    5.142      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3095:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201417 and revision id 227838. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}